    "title": "Game Of Thrones Star's New Sci-Fi Movie Changes The Rules Of A Popular Genre",
    "text": "Published Mar 31, 2026, 5:09 PM EDT Felipe Rangel is a Movie and TV Journalist ScreenRant. He has been writing about movies and TV since 2021. Felipe joined ScreenRant in 2022, working across different teams, covering everything from breaking news to features to reviews and more. Felipe is a writer who is an avid film and TV fan, with superhero movies and series being his biggest passion. He graduated from college in 2019, having studied Journalism. Before college, he spent a month studying at the Oxford English Centre. His superhero knowledge expands to the comics, with his undergraduate thesis being \"Politics Reflected In American Comics.\" Sign in to your ScreenRant account Game of Thrones fans will soon see one of the franchise's brightest stars in an epic sci-fi movie that looks like a blast and changes the rules of another popular franchise and genre. As a long-running series with eight seasons, Game of Thrones' cast has quite a few stars who have gone on to appear in hit projects. The larger franchise works similarly. Game of Thrones spinoffs like House of the Dragon and A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms have found immense success and birthed new stars. One of them happens to be leading an entry in the list of the most exciting 2026 sci-fi movies. Now, after that film's first full trailer, it has become clear that the movie is a win for another genre. DC's Supergirl Movie Trailer Puts The Focus On Its Sci-Fi Elements The first full Supergirl movie trailer focused on the DC film's sci-fi elements, firmly making it more of an entry for that genre than a traditional superhero flick. Nine planets will appear in the movie, with some of them spotlighted in the trailer, and Krypton's destruction serving to showcase how this is a truly space-based Supergirl adventure. Spaceships, alien races, advanced technology, and more appear. Supergirl Is DC's First Live-Action Movie To Go Full Space Epic The reason for that is that Supergirl presents a journey across several different planets that likely do not even feature Earth, aside from Superman-related scenes. The 2026 DC movie is a planet-hopping journey that is more akin to what Marvel has accomplished before with the Guardians of the Galaxy franchise than any of DC's live-action movies thus far. Sure, at its core, Supergirl is a superhero movie. However, for those who lean more into sci-fi than the superhero genre, the DC movie is a true space epic that can be watched without any past superhero knowledge. Supergirl will venture into space with Ruthye, her companion, to get an antidote to save the dying Krypto. Release Date June 26, 2026 Director Craig Gillespie Writers Ana Nogueira, Otto Binder, Tom King, Al Plastino, Jerry Siegel, Joe Shuster, Bilquis Evely Cast Matthias Schoenaerts Krem of the Yellow Hills Eve Ridley Ruthye Mary Knolle",
